This is an idea that came to me a few days ago. Sorry if it's already been=
=20
suggested or already exists, or if this is the wrong place (the lojban=20
GGroup throws an error (#554) if I try to post there) or I've committed=20
some faux pas.

I think there should be a cmavo for quoting a gesture or graphical symbol.=
=20
I'll call it {zo'ai} by analogy to {zo'oi} but with the =E2=80=98a=E2=80=99=
 of {xance} and=20
{sinxa}. It could have selma'o KOhA, unless it needs something zo'oi-like=
=20
for written symbols.

Slightly more formally, the end of {zo'ai} begins the quote, and the next=
=20
spoken/orthographical word ends it. Here are two equivalent examples:

   - la'e zo'ai (*points right*) smuni zo pritu
   - la'e zo'ai =E2=86=92 smuni zo pritu

It does break AVI (audio-visual isomorphism), but when talking about, say,=
=20
sign language (without using a specialist notation), it will be broken=20
anyway (probably more so, since the written version will refer to an image=
=20
outside the text). To stick closer to AVI, maybe {zo'ai} should accept=20
{sei} (or at least some SEI) afterwards to allow a description of the=20
action, which overrides any action observed in case of conflict. So we get:

   - la'e zo'ai sei pritu degja'o cu smuni zo pritu
  =20
.i pei .i mu'o mi'e mudri

